      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the number of ways Johnny can choose 3 marbles out of 7, we use the combination formula:\n\n\\[\nC(n, k) = \\frac{n!}{k! \\, (n - k)!}\n\\]\n\nwhere $n$ is the total number of items to choose from, $k$ is the number of items to choose, and $n!$ represents the factorial of $n$ (the product of all positive integers up to $n$).\n\nHere, $n = 7$ and $k = 3$ since Johnny wants to choose 3 marbles out of the 7. Applying the formula:\n\n\\[\nC(7, 3) = \\frac{7!}{(3!\\, (7-3)!)} = \\frac{7!}{(3!\\, 4!)}\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the calculation:\n\n\\[\n7! = 7 \\times 6 \\times 5 \\times 4!\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\nC(7, 3) = \\frac{7 \\times 6 \\times 5 \\times 4!}{3! \\times 4!}\n\\]\n\nObserve that the $4!$ terms in the numerator and denominator cancel out:\n\n\\[\nC(7, 3) = \\frac{7 \\times 6 \\times 5}{3!} = \\frac{7 \\times 6 \\times 5}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\n\nNow calculate the remaining part:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{7 \\times 6 \\times 5}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{210}{6} = 35\n\\]\n\nThus, Johnny can choose 3 marbles in 35 different ways. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{35}\n\\]",
